---

### Program.cs (stdio transport + DI setup)

```csharp
var builder = Host.CreateApplicationBuilder(args);

// Logs → stderr only. stdout is the MCP JSON-RPC channel.
builder.Logging.AddConsole(o => o.LogToStandardErrorThreshold = LogLevel.Trace);

// Register named HttpClient — injected into tool classes via IHttpClientFactory
builder.Services.AddHttpClient("api", client =>
{
    client.BaseAddress = new Uri("https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com");
});

builder.Services
    .AddMcpServer()
    .WithStdioServerTransport()
    .WithToolsFromAssembly();  // auto-discovers all [McpServerToolType] classes

await builder.Build().RunAsync();
```

### ApiTools.cs (tool class wrapping REST API)

The class uses **constructor injection** — `IHttpClientFactory` and `ILogger<T>` are resolved by DI and *never* appear in the tool schema. Only parameters with `[Description]` are exposed to the LLM.

```csharp
[McpServerToolType]
public class ApiTools(IHttpClientFactory httpFactory, ILogger<ApiTools> logger)
{
    [McpServerTool, Description("Get a post by its ID from the REST API.")]
    public async Task<string> GetPost(
        [Description("The numeric post ID (1–100).")] int id,
        CancellationToken cancellationToken = default) { ... }

    [McpServerTool, Description("List posts, optionally filtered by user ID.")]
    public async Task<string> ListPosts(
        [Description("Filter by user ID.")] int? userId = null,
        CancellationToken cancellationToken = default) { ... }

    [McpServerTool, Description("Create a new post via the REST API.")]
    public async Task<string> CreatePost(
        [Description("Author user ID.")] int userId,
        [Description("Post title.")] string title,
        [Description("Post body text.")] string body,
        CancellationToken cancellationToken = default) { ... }
}
```

### How DI works for MCP tools

The SDK has **two injection styles**:

| Style | How it works |
|-------|-------------|
| **Constructor injection** (non-static class) | Services like `HttpClient`, `ILogger<T>` are injected via the primary constructor. The SDK instantiates the class per-call using the DI container. |
| **Method parameter injection** (static class) | DI services can appear directly as method parameters. The SDK distinguishes them from tool inputs — only parameters with `[Description]` become part of the schema. |

These types are **always auto-injected** and hidden from the LLM: `CancellationToken`, `IMcpServer`, `IProgress<ProgressNotificationValue>`, and any DI-registered service.

The project is at `ApiMcpServer/` and builds cleanly.
